we've recently discussed the four Titan  brothers who have personified as the  four pillars of the earth because of the  role they played during Uranus's  castration today we take a look at the  Titan Hyperion who was regarded as the  pillar of the east and the God of  heavenly light Hyperion is one of the  first generation of titans born from  Gaia and Uranus and along with his wife  Thea  he was commonly known as lady of the  aether the shine in blue within the sky  they were both heavily associated with  the heavens and the light source it  provided the earth  Hyperion's name itself can be roughly  translated to watch her from above or he  who goes from above and he was thought  to represent watchfulness wisdom and  light it's quite a common sentiment in  mythology as well as religion that the  gods watched us mortals from the heavens  above it's not much of a surprise that  the children of Hyperion and Thea were  also closely linked to the heavens in  the sky Helios the Titan of the Sun  Selene the Titan goddess of the moon and  yaws the Titan goddess of dawn over the  years there has been some ambiguity  between Hyperion and his connection to  the Sun when we think of a heavenly  light source it's natural for us to  assume that that could only refer to the  Sun or the moon and in some of the early  texts such as Homer's Iliad and the  Odyssey the Sun was referred to as  Helios Hyperion almost implying that  Hyperion could in fact be the Sun in the  later texts of Hesiod's Theogony the Sun  was referred to as Hyperion Hades  meaning the Sun of Hyperion this could  refer to the Sun being a creation of  Hyperion or it could indeed refer to  Helios but what does Theogony does is  separate the Sun from Hyperion they  described as two separate things  Hyperion being shown as his own physical  being in the text that subsequently  followed there was always a clear  distinction made between Hyperion and  his son Hyperion was often associated  with the characteristics of wisdom and  light and ultimately known as the god of  watchfulness Helios on the other hand  was often seen as the physical  incarnation of the Sun  Hyperion is another Titan that doesn't  really feature much in Greek mythology  and during the war between the Titans  and Olympians he is hardly mentioned at  all we can only assume that he was  amongst the Titans imprisoned by Zeus in  Tartarus there are those who believe  that Hyperion been a deity of the  heavens meant that he was able to  observe far more than the other Titans  and gods and because of his diligent  observation he was the first to truly  understand the movements of the Sun and  the moon as well as the stars in the  seasons it's believed that it was  Hyperion who ordered the cycles of the  Sun the moon and the dome given time and  organized structure and helping us  create our own concept of the different  times within a day also allowed us to  track the times of the month in the year  during the creation of man it's believed  that the Titans each bestowed man with  one of their own qualities Hyperion in  his wife Thea being deities of light in  the sky gave man the gift of sight  although Hyperion doesn't play a huge  role in the stories of Greek mythology  he was quite an important figure  nonetheless not only because he was one  of the first forms of light when the  world was created from chaos but because  his observations meant that he created  the cycles of night and day he's  children the dawn the Sun and the moon  symbolize in the different periods of  the day itself he also gave the ancient  Greeks a way to measure the seasons with  these different cycles during the year  something that would be extremely valued  by farmers and anyone whose livelihood  was dependent on the weather in the time  of year  Hyperion gives us this figure of an ever  vigilant and observing watcher from  above the type of God that people who  aren't familiar with mythology would  associate the term God with but I'd like  to hear what you guys think were you  familiar with the role Hyperion played  in Greek mythology or when you think of  gods associated of the Sun and the skies  do you think of Apollo and Zeus instead  let me know in the comments below as  always I've been your host mythology and  fiction explained
 

